Full job description
Microsoft 365 IT Engineer

Keep the infrastructure that powers next-gen manufacturing secure, connected, and running. Are you ready to own the Microsoft 365 environment at a company building software for aerospace, space exploration, and advanced manufacturing?
At Manufacturo, your work keeps the digital backbone running for pioneers like Sierra Space, Relativity Space, and Hermeus. Every user account you secure, every endpoint you protect, every automation you build — it all directly enables the people launching rockets and redefining manufacturing.

Why Join Manufacturo? This isn’t just another IT admin role. It’s an opportunity to:

Work alongside former SpaceX experts and immerse yourself in the space and advanced manufacturing industry.
Thrive in a fast-paced, agile environment where your IT decisions directly protect and enable critical engineering work.
Contribute to infrastructure with real impact — your security configurations and automations support humanity’s most ambitious manufacturing projects.
We’re seeking a hands-on, curious, and driven Microsoft 365 IT Engineer eager to own a modern cloud environment end-to-end.

Required Skills & Experience

Proven professional experience administering and operating Microsoft 365 in enterprise environments.
Managing user accounts, licenses, and permissions in accordance with IT policies.
Strong expertise with: Microsoft 365, Azure Active Directory, Exchange Online, Microsoft Teams, SharePoint Online, OneDrive for Business, Microsoft Entra ID (including Enterprise Applications and App Registrations).
Design, implement, and optimize Microsoft Defender for Endpoint solutions — strong understanding of threat detection, incident response, and endpoint protection.
Collaborate with the IT team to deliver end-to-end security solutions.
Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues in a timely manner such as email delivery failures or authentication problems.
Manage the deployment of new features and functionality of the M365 product suite.
Provide support for end users experiencing problems with Office 365 applications and services.
Produce clear technical documentation for architecture, configurations, and security decisions.
PowerShell scripting skills for automation.
Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with a structured, solution-oriented approach.
Excellent communication skills and the ability to explain technical concepts to non-technical stakeholders.
You will get extra points if you have

Experience with Microsoft Graph API.
Network management background.
Experience building scalable automation and operational improvements.
Ability to take ownership, proactively identify improvement opportunities, and drive initiatives independently.
Experience working in complex enterprise environments.
What you'll be working on
You’ll work closely with a cross-functional IT team to keep Manufacturo’s Microsoft cloud environment secure, reliable, and continuously improving. Our teams follow agile practices with a focus on delivering value quickly while maintaining high-quality standards. You’ll own your domain end-to-end — from day-to-day administration and user support, to designing security solutions and building automations that make the whole team more effective.

